/-!
# A reflector and a generator of the pulling salvo

Components of the machine design D1 (research notes `N-10`, `N-11`, `N-15`) found by the
project's own search (`scripts/life_machine`, report
`notes/research/reports/R-21-salvo-generators.md`) and certified here.

* `reflector`: a queen bee shuttle (the left half of the Gosper gun) with an eater. It is an
  oscillator of period exactly 30 (`reflector_isOscillator`) and turns a glider by a right angle
  (`reflector_reflects`).
* `pullGenerator`: an assembly of six guns (three blocked pairs) and three reflectors, periodic
  with period 30 (`pullGenerator_evolve_thirty`). One control glider `pullGeneratorControl`
  makes it emit exactly the pulling salvo of the sliding block memory, after which it is back in
  its cycle:
  `pullGenerator_reaction :
    Reaction (pullGenerator ∪ pullGeneratorControl)
      (pullGenerator ∪ translate (51, 143) pullSalvo) 1170 (fun _ => Box (-86) 90 (-9) 152)`.
  During all 1170 generations the whole configuration stays in the stated box, so a block
  below row 152 is not disturbed while the salvo is produced.

How it works (observations of the search, not part of what is proved): the control glider opens
a gate; the released glider is kicked back by a second gun pair, which releases a glider itself;
the returning glider opens the first gate once more; the two gliders obtained are brought to the
lanes of the salvo, six apart, by a third gate and three reflectors. Only the input–output
statement above is certified; the internal mechanism is not stated.

The certificate is split into 9 parts of 130 generations (`pullGenerator_part_*`), each proved
by `life_reaction` with the same box, and composed with `Reaction.seq_const`.

**Sanity.** `reflector_isOscillator` (without a glider the reflector emits nothing),
`pullGenerator_evolve_thirty` (without a control glider the generator emits nothing).
-/

